# role               model    effort   window  opencode-model     opencode-effort   — read by scripts/fleet-up; aliases: fable, opus, sonnet, haiku
# Cheap by default (target about $10 per person per day): sonnet everywhere, opus only where judgement is the
# job (project-manager, which reads every peer and routes their questions; architect; spec-reviewer).
# window: the peer's auto-compact window in tokens (CLAUDE_CODE_AUTO_COMPACT_WINDOW); blank = the model's full
# window. Claude Code only: a Cursor peer (cli agent) ignores model, effort and window; Cursor sets its own.
# opencode-model/opencode-effort (cols 5–6): OpenRouter model ID and reasoning effort for a peer that runs
# FLEET_CLI=opencode (through Ori's launcher); blank = the peer's own OpenCode model selection applies.
# Never set CLAUDE_AUTOCOMPACT_PCT_OVERRIDE (globally or here): a peer's baseline is ~75K tokens, so 25% of a
# 200K window traps every peer in compaction from its first turn.
project-manager      opus     medium   500000
architect            opus     high     500000
pr-architect         sonnet   medium
security-architect   sonnet   medium
designer             sonnet   medium
engineer             sonnet   low      150000
dev-support          sonnet   low      150000
e2e-engineer         sonnet   medium
performance-engineer sonnet   medium
ba                   sonnet   medium
spec-reviewer        opus     high     500000
jira                 haiku    low
